#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:16
msgid "Overview and using RQt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:19
msgid ""
"RQt provides a flexible graphical framework for running ROS tools and "
"plugins in a shared, dockable interface. This article introduces RQt, "
"explains how to run available plugins, and describes the main components and "
"advantages of using the RQt framework."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:28
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:31
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:33
msgid ""
"RQt is a graphical user interface framework that implements various tools "
"and interfaces in the form of plugins. One can run all the existing GUI "
"tools as dockable windows within RQt. The tools can still run in a "
"traditional standalone method, but RQt makes it easier to manage all the "
"various windows in a single screen layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:37
msgid "You can run any RQt tools/plugins easily by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:39
msgid "$ rqt"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:43
msgid ""
"This GUI allows you to choose any available plugins on your system. You can "
"also run plugins in standalone windows. For example, RQt Python Console:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:47
msgid "$ ros2 run rqt_py_console rqt_py_console"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:51
msgid ""
"Users can create their own plugins for RQt with either ``Python`` or ``C+"
"+``. To see what RQt plugins are available for your system, run:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:54
msgid "$ ros2 pkg list"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Visualization/About-RQt.rst:58
msgid "And then look for packages that start with ``rqt_``."
msgstr ""

